ok - reclaim: a herdr rebind is created in the session the record names, never the ambient one
ok - reclaim: a herdr rebind refuses to publish a record whose pane reads back another terminal than the create returned
ok - reclaim: a herdr rebind that cannot read its pane identity leaves the pane open and names it
ok - reclaim: a herdr pane that outlived its stopped server is adopted, never orphaned beside a new tab
ok - reclaim: a herdr agent that came back with its server refuses, so one worktree keeps one agent
ok - reclaim: a herdr reclaim rebinds the endpoint and leaves the whole rest of the task alone
ok - fm-control relaunch: a same-harness relaunch replaces the agent in the same endpoint and worktree
